# Kiosk service (per-machine, contains plaintext password)
dart-games-service.exe
dart-games-service.xml
logs/service/
server/bin/server.exe

# Windows plugin registrants — regenerated by `flutter pub get` on every
# checkout. Cross-platform developers' pub gets kept flipping the line
# endings CRLF <-> LF and (occasionally) reordering plugins, producing
# noise-only diffs. Nothing depends on these being tracked: `flutter
# build windows` / `flutter run -d windows` regenerate them from
# pubspec.lock. We never ship Windows binaries — the kiosk deploy is
# a web build served by the Dart server.
windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.cc
windows/flutter/generated_plugin_registrant.h
windows/flutter/generated_plugins.cmake

# ChromeDriver — a 60 MB binary payload that is downloaded, not authored.
# `update_chromedriver.bat` fetches the build matching the locally installed
# Chrome and writes all four files (chromedriver.exe, the zip it came in,
# LICENSE and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES). Tracking them meant every driver update
# landed as a 60 MB binary diff, and a machine whose Chrome had auto-updated
# showed a permanently dirty working tree it could not meaningfully commit.
#
# Nothing needs them in git: run_ui_tests_parallel.bat calls
# update_chromedriver.bat before every run, and that script bootstraps from
# nothing — a missing driver reports major version 0, which forces the
# download and creates the directories it extracts into.
chromedriver/
